CMake helps to "give a mental model" your project for the your esp. It processes your files, links stuff etc. This is to "tell" your esp idf your project structure. So very different from compilation.
components are for your files that you coded and will reuse
sdkconfig are preconfigured settings. the saved settings that are configured using sdkconfig.default. the skdconfig.h and .cpp are different structures for if you want to port it to different environment
bootloader_components are for external components that you will download
dependencies.lock are the saved info/metadata (yeah.. that should be the right word)
Kconfig is the config file. Containing the settings you want to modify.. 
idf_component.yml is the file that describes the descriptive information/metadata of the component you want to port using the IDF Component Manager.
IDF Component Manager is what you use to download and manage external esp components.
